{% if ml_stack == 'analysis' %}
{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    {{ ('# ' + project_name + ' — baseline model') | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "A scikit-learn baseline on the processed data from `01-explore-data.ipynb`. Beat\n",
    "this before reaching for anything bigger.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import joblib\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }} import data\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.config import MODELS_DIR\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.config import RANDOM_SEED\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.config import ensure_dirs\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.seeding import set_seed\n",
    "\n",
    "ensure_dirs()\n",
    "set_seed()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Split\n",
    "\n",
    "The split lives in `data.split_train_valid_test`, not in the notebook: every notebook that\n",
    "imports it gets exactly the same test set."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "frame = data.load_processed('dataset.parquet')\n",
    "train, valid, test = data.split_train_valid_test(frame, stratify_on='target')\n",
    "features = ['feature_a', 'feature_b']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'train={len(train)} valid={len(valid)} test={len(test)}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Fit\n",
    "\n",
    "The scaler is inside the `Pipeline`, so it is fitted on the training fold only and travels\n",
    "with the model when it is saved."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = Pipeline(\n",
    "    [\n",
    "        ('scale', StandardScaler()),\n",
    "        ('forest', RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=300, random_state=RANDOM_SEED)),\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")\n",
    "model.fit(train[features], train['target'])\n",
    "\n",
    "valid_accuracy = accuracy_score(valid['target'], model.predict(valid[features]))\n",
    "print(f'valid accuracy: {valid_accuracy:.3f}')"
   ]
  },
{% if experiment_tracking != 'none' %}
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.tracking import log_metrics\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.tracking import start_run\n",
    "\n",
    "with start_run('random-forest-baseline', {'n_estimators': 300, 'seed': RANDOM_SEED}):\n",
    "    log_metrics({'valid_accuracy': valid_accuracy})"
   ]
  },
{% endif %}
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Evaluate once, on the test set\n",
    "\n",
    "Only after the model is settled: every look at the test set spends a little of its value as\n",
    "an estimate of real performance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(classification_report(test['target'], model.predict(test[features])))\n",
    "\n",
    "path = MODELS_DIR / 'baseline.joblib'\n",
    "joblib.dump(model, path)\n",
    "print(f'saved {path}')"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "metadata": {
  "kernelspec": {
   "display_name": "Python 3",
   "language": "python",
   "name": "python3"
  },
  "language_info": {
   "name": "python",
   "version": "3"
  }
 },
 "nbformat": 4,
 "nbformat_minor": 5
}
{% endif %}
{% if ml_stack == 'deep-learning' %}
{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    {{ ('# ' + project_name + ' — PyTorch training') | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "The loop itself lives in `src/{{ package_import_name }}/training.py` so it can be tested and\n",
    "re-run from a script; the notebook is where the model and the hyper-parameters\n",
    "are chosen.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "from torch import nn\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader\n",
    "\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }} import training\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.config import ensure_dirs\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.seeding import set_seed\n",
    "\n",
    "ensure_dirs()\n",
    "set_seed()\n",
    "device = training.resolve_device()\n",
    "print(f'training on {device}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Data\n",
    "\n",
    "`synthetic_datasets` keeps this notebook runnable offline. Swap in a real `Dataset` (or a\n",
    "`TensorDataset` built from `data.load_processed(...)`) and nothing below changes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "train_dataset, valid_dataset = training.synthetic_datasets(rows=2048, features=16)\n",
    "valid_loader = DataLoader(valid_dataset, batch_size=64)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'train={len(train_dataset)} valid={len(valid_dataset)}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "    nn.Linear(16, 64),\n",
    "    nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "    nn.Dropout(0.1),\n",
    "    nn.Linear(64, 1),\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()), 'parameters')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Train\n",
    "\n",
    "Per-epoch losses are printed{% if experiment_tracking != 'none' %} and logged to the tracker{% endif %}, and\n",
    "the weights are checkpointed into `models/` (gitignored)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "config = training.TrainingConfig(epochs=10, batch_size=64, learning_rate=1e-3)\n",
    "checkpoint = training.train(\n",
    "    model,\n",
    "    train_dataset,\n",
    "    valid_dataset,\n",
    "    config,\n",
    "    run_name='mlp-baseline',\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(checkpoint)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Evaluate and reload\n",
    "\n",
    "Reloading the checkpoint into a fresh model is the cheapest way to find out that what was\n",
    "saved is what you think it is."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "reloaded = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "    nn.Linear(16, 64),\n",
    "    nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "    nn.Dropout(0.1),\n",
    "    nn.Linear(64, 1),\n",
    ")\n",
    "reloaded.load_state_dict(torch.load(checkpoint, map_location=device))\n",
    "reloaded.to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "loss = training.evaluate(reloaded, valid_loader, nn.MSELoss(), device)\n",
    "print(f'valid loss: {loss:.4f}')"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "metadata": {
  "kernelspec": {
   "display_name": "Python 3",
   "language": "python",
   "name": "python3"
  },
  "language_info": {
   "name": "python",
   "version": "3"
  }
 },
