{% if ml_stack == 'transformers' %}
{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    {{ ('# ' + project_name + ' — transformer fine-tuning') | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Fine-tunes a pretrained sequence classifier with the Hugging Face `Trainer`. The\n",
    "model and the dataset are downloaded from the Hub on first use and cached, so the\n",
    "first run needs network access (`huggingface.co` is on the egress allowlist when\n",
    "the firewall is enabled).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "from datasets import load_dataset\n",
    "from transformers import AutoTokenizer\n",
    "from transformers import pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }} import training\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.config import ensure_dirs\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.seeding import set_seed\n",
    "\n",
    "ensure_dirs()\n",
    "set_seed()\n",
    "\n",
    "MODEL_NAME = 'distilbert-base-uncased'\n",
    "print(f'device: {training.resolve_device()}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Dataset and tokenizer\n",
    "\n",
    "Look at the raw text and at what the tokenizer turns it into before training on it: this is\n",
    "where truncation length and label mapping mistakes show up."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "dataset = load_dataset('imdb')\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_NAME)\n",
    "\n",
    "example = dataset['train'][0]\n",
    "print(example['label'], example['text'][:300])\n",
    "print(tokenizer(example['text'], truncation=True, max_length=32))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Fine-tune\n",
    "\n",
    "`train_size` subsamples the training split so the first run finishes in minutes on a CPU;\n",
    "pass `train_size=None` for the full dataset (and use a GPU for it)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "output_dir = training.fine_tune_text_classifier(\n",
    "    dataset_name='imdb',\n",
    "    model_name=MODEL_NAME,\n",
    "    train_size=2000,\n",
    "    config=training.TrainingConfig(epochs=1, batch_size=16, learning_rate=2e-5),\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(output_dir)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Try it\n",
    "\n",
    "The saved directory holds the weights *and* the tokenizer, so it can be loaded as a\n",
    "pipeline directly — that is what deployment will do."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "classifier = pipeline(\n",
    "    'text-classification',\n",
    "    model=str(output_dir),\n",
    "    device=0 if torch.cuda.is_available() else -1,\n",
    ")\n",
    "classifier(\n",
    "    [\n",
    "        'A quietly devastating film, and the best thing I have seen this year.',\n",
    "        'Two hours I will never get back.',\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")"
   ]
  }
 ],
